+# Daily Grind rewards registration
+
+Requires Node.js 24+. Install dependencies with `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`.
+`pnpm build` checks syntax; `pnpm test` runs cryptographic and handler tests without
+starting HTTP servers. `pnpm start` runs the application when you are ready to serve it.
+
+## Production configuration
+
+Supply environment variables using your hosting platform (see `.env.example`;
+the app does not automatically load `.env` files):
+
+- `PUBLIC_ORIGIN`: exact public HTTPS origin, without a trailing slash. Token
+  audiences and POST origins are checked against this value; proxy headers and
+  request hostnames are never trusted to select the audience.
+- `EMAIL_VERIFICATION_ORIGIN_TRIAL_TOKEN`: register the public origin for Chrome's
+  [Email Verification origin trial](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/identity/email-verification/verifier).
+  The server sends this as an `Origin-Trial` response header. No trial token is
+  included in the repository. Use an up-to-date token for the trial extension.
+- `EVP_TRUSTED_ORIGINS`: operator-approved HTTPS origins for both issuer discovery
+  and JWKS retrieval. Defaults support Google's issuer and JWKS service. Add other
+  participating providers after reviewing their discovery/JWKS origins. The email
+  domain must also delegate the exact issuer via `_email-verification` DNS TXT.
+- `DATABASE_PATH`: persistent SQLite file (default `data/rewards.sqlite`). Protect
+  this file and its directory: they contain personal data, password hashes, and
+  temporary session secrets. Deploy as one Node service with persistent storage;
+  this is not an ephemeral/serverless or replicated database configuration.
+
+## Registration behavior
+
+The homepage is rendered per request with a random nonce and separate CSRF token.
+A random opaque HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite=Lax cookie identifies server-side
+session state. Sessions expire after ten minutes, and submission atomically
+deletes the session before verification, preventing concurrent replay. Local HTTP
+uses an unprefixed non-Secure cookie for development only.
+
+The form uses native POST submission so the browser can populate its hidden
+`autocomplete="email-verification-token"` input. Browser support, a participating
+provider, an active provider session, permission, HTTPS, and origin-trial enrollment
+are required. Verification uses `@sd-jwt/core` and `jose` for issuer and holder
+signatures, token freshness, email match, audience, nonce, and SD-JWT digest binding.
+Network retrieval is HTTPS-only, allowlisted, size-limited, timeout-bound, and
+rejects redirects. Only verified submissions create accounts; passwords are salted
+and hashed with scrypt, and email uniqueness is case-insensitive.
+
+No OTP, magic link, or other verification email is sent. Unsupported browsers,
+missing tokens, invalid tokens, or unavailable providers receive an actionable
+retry message and a fresh form; they are never treated as verified. This deliberate
+fail-closed behavior follows the requested no-email policy rather than the API's
+usual emailed fallback. Names and email addresses are preserved on retry; passwords
+and verification tokens are not echoed. Account registration is implemented here;
+the site's existing account, login, and reward redemption pages remain separate work.
+
+At the edge, apply request-rate and abuse limits appropriate to your deployment.
+The origin trial is experimental; monitor provider and browser changes before
+expanding support.
